<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bimaal</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Biimaal</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bimaal are a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somalis">Somali</a> clan of the Dir family living in the coastal region around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marka">Merca</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somalia">Somalia</a>. In the 19th century they were rivals of the Geledi sultanate, and in 1878 they killed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmed-yusuf-of-geledi">Ahmed Yusuf</a> in battle. They later resisted Italian colonial rule on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benadir">Benadir coast</a> in the early 20th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bimaal.jpg" alt="Bimaal" width="320" height="202" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown. Dated 1938; Sawir ku taariikhaysan 1938, waxuu u badan yahay in the mudda ka qaaday horraysa taariikhdaas, loona … · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Notables_belong_to_the_Biimaal_clan.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
